SUMMARY:Zoetropolis Pride Collection: The Queen & Amish Country Queer
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Pride at Zoetropolis with a special double-feature screening highlighting drag history and local queer culture. The evening kicks off with a screening of Amish Country Queer\, an award-winning short documentary that explores Lancaster’s vibrant queer nightlife and drag scene. Followed by the 1968 documentary The Queen\, where viewers will go behind the scenes of the 1967 Miss All-American Camp Beauty Pageant in New York City\, capturing the dressing room camaraderie\, rehearsals\, and tension of a foundational era in drag history.
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/zoetropolis-pride-collection-the-queen-amish-country-queer/
LOCATION:Zoetropolis Cinema Stillhouse\, 112 North Water Street\, Lancaster\, Pennsylvania\, 17603\, United States
END:VEVENT
